# Call-site ledger of pluggy at 4c7f6365f2dde09c11e72db67d0f615231d64c19.
# Hand-written from the source; judgements and statistics in pluggy.md.
#
# Recurring facts that the reasons below refer to:
# - The hook relay (PluginManager.hook, a HookRelay) holds only HookCallers:
#   the package sets its attributes only at _manager.py:248 and :357, both
#   with a HookCaller. A _SubsetHookCaller exists only as the return value of
#   PluginManager.subset_hook_caller (_manager.py:648), given to the client.
# - Plugins, hook specification namespaces, hook implementation functions,
#   hook arguments and results, call_extra methods, result callbacks, trace
#   arguments, writers and processors are objects of the client. The API
#   takes any object there; the package passes none of its own objects in
#   these roles, so their special methods are client code (see pluggy.md,
#   "Objects of the client").
# - HookCaller.__repr__, _SubsetHookCaller.__repr__ and HookImpl.__repr__ are
#   the only package methods that formatting can reach.
default reject pluggy._caller.HookRelay.__getattr__: defined only under `if TYPE_CHECKING:` (_caller.py:42-44), which does not run, so HookRelay has no __getattr__ at run time
default reject pluggy.__getattr__: the module __getattr__ of `pluggy` runs only for an attribute that the module's dict lacks, on the module object `pluggy` itself; no package code names that module after __init__.py:32 defines the function (the relative imports of the submodules run earlier, during the import of the package), and a receiver that the client supplies (a plugin, a hook function, a namespace of hook specifications) is never that module: it would be an arbitrary package object where any object, callable, module or class is accepted (rule B3)
default reject pluggy._compat.DistFacade.__getattr__: runs only for an attribute that normal lookup does not find on a DistFacade instance; at _compat.py 39:29 and 43:32 the receiver is a DistFacade, but the attribute is the slot _dist, which __init__ always sets, so normal lookup finds it; at every other site that this default decides, the receiver is not a DistFacade: DistFacade instances come only from list_plugin_distinfo (_manager.py:539), which gives them to the client, and a client that passes one where any object is accepted (as a plugin or a hook function) passes an arbitrary package object (rule B3)

